  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM&apos;s Human Trafficking Information Exchange: A Reliable Foundation for Effective Anti-Trafficking Policies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is preparing its victim database for public use, including appropriate safeguards to prevent the disclosure of victims personally-identifiable information. The database, a unique tool which monitors assistance and collects information on IOM-assisted trafficking victims, is the largest repository of primary, single-case data on assisted trafficked persons.</narrative>
  </description>
